        ("Will the swarm on my tree leave by itself?", "Often, yes. A resting swarm is waiting for its scouts to agree on a new home, and that can take a few hours or a few days. Trouble starts when the scouts vote for a hollow in your own attic or wall. If you need the bees gone sooner, or you notice them entering the house, ask for a pickup instead of waiting."),
